## What was built (see PR description for the full list)

- Migration `20260801120500_f44_version_list_and_derived.sql`: per-version creator_kind /
  agent_run_id / change_source on `artifact_versions`; `pipeline_version` +
  nullable-except-embedding `object_storage_key` on `derived_representations`.
- `ArtifactRepository.listVersions` / `.createDerived` / `.listDerived` (port + Postgres impl).
- `uploadNewVersion` (idempotent re-upload, optimistic concurrency, reuses `materializeArtifact`).
- `createDerivedRepresentation` (rerun-safe: new row + new object key per generation, embedding
  registered without a file).
- `versionContentHash` factored out of `materializeArtifact` so `uploadNewVersion`'s idempotency
  check uses the exact same hash formula as the write path (a bug caught by this feature's own
  V2 test -- see PR description).
- Web: `tests/ui/files-version-derived.test.tsx` against the already-built `version-drawer.tsx`
  (F44's UI-first predecessor) proves the version-list/derived-file behaviour the contract and
  `user_visible_behavior` describe, at the component level (same technique as F32's
  `files-preview.test.tsx`).

## Known gap, reported rather than silently left implicit

No HTTP controller / route registration for `listVersions` / `uploadNewVersion` / `listDerived`
is included -- the contract's `GET /artifacts/:artifactId/file-versions` etc. exist in
`packages/contracts/src/files.ts` but nothing in `apps/api/src/interface/controllers` wires them
yet, and `version-drawer.tsx` still reads from `lib/mock/files.ts`, not a live endpoint. This
feature's three required verification commands exercise the repository/application layer
directly (the same pattern `no-orphan-version.test.ts` and `pin-version` tests already use), and
the issue's `user_visible_behavior` is satisfied by the UI as already built against mock data.
Wiring the controllers is real, separately-sized work (auth, DTO validation, route registration)
that no test in this feature's scope requires, and inventing it untested would be exactly the
"looks done, isn't verified" failure mode this repository's CLAUDE.md warns about. Left for the
feature that actually wires the browser to the backend, flagged explicitly rather than silently
assumed.
